    13	| MAI-UI-2B **Q8_0** (1.83 GB) | `<thinking>\nThought: To turn the brightness to the maximum, I should open Settings, navigate to Displ…` (58 tokens) | `Thought: I should open Settings, go to Display, and set Brightness…` (46 tokens) |
    14	| MAI-UI-2B **Q4_K_M** (1.11 GB) | `<thinking>\n<thinking>\n<thinking>\n</thinking>…` (hit the cap) | same (hit the cap) |
    15	
    16	Q4_K_M behaviour depends on tiny input changes (704x1568, 768x1696 or a JPEG-recompressed copy of the same screenshot
    17	were fine), i.e. the first token after `<thinking>` sits on a knife edge after 4-bit quantization. GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (same
    18	Qwen3-VL architecture) and LFM3 v4 do not show this at Q4_K_M. Both GGUFs were converted from Tongyi-MAI/MAI-UI-2B @
    19	5030509 with llama.cpp cd959bae9; the chat template is the standard Qwen3-VL one.
    20	
    21	Decision: MAI-UI's AndroidWorld arm runs at **Q8_0** (everything else matched: one screenshot <= 1,048,576 px, temperature
    22	0, same server flags). This gives MAI-UI a precision advantage over the Q4_K_M v4 and GUI-Owl arms; it is reported as
    23	such. The smoke check now also fails if more than a quarter of the steps have an empty `<thinking>`.
