+| v4 failure | 16 | 83 |
+
+The v4-minus-GUI-Owl difference is **−15.238095 percentage points**. The two-sided exact McNemar value is `2 × (1/2)^16 = 1/32768 = 0.000030517578125`; the saved `3.05e-05` is correct. The original 97-task sensitivity also reproduces under its narrower definition; finding 3 explains the reporting mismatch and broader calculation. Treat the p-value as conditional on this task-pair analysis, not a measurement of seed-to-seed uncertainty or a causal separation of model and harness effects. The artifacts already label the benchmark secondary/descriptive; no claim of a preregistered primary endpoint was found.
+
+**Retry policy and symmetry.** The two `classify()` implementations agree for every no-result folder among all **241 attempt folders**. Resume checks result existence outside its classifier, while the summarizer checks it inside; that is not a disagreement. Every current attempt folder has one thread log, so lexicographic concatenation of multiple thread logs causes no misclassification in this snapshot.
+
+The extracted dry planner returns no work for v4 and exactly ThanksgivingPrepTask for GUI-Owl. GUI-Owl's SendInterviewEmailTask and CheckInvoiceTask2 remain final failures. Only v4 has a moved folder and retry manifest in this snapshot; that matches GUI-Owl's explicitly pending resume, rather than proving unequal application of the rule. The manifest contains the executed `rerun` decision; the later dry completion check does not append a final-failure decision. Completion audit trails should retain that final disposition as well.
+
+MW's outer retry logic re-executes tasks returning `None`, not ordinary tasks scored zero ([runner.py:351](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/tools/MobileWorld/src/mobile_world/core/runner.py:351)); a valid result file is skipped on later scans ([client.py:418](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/tools/MobileWorld/src/mobile_world/runtime/client.py:418)). GUI-Owl's 24 replaced folders comprise 11 setup/scoring failures, 6 unavailable-simulator failures, 5 unsupported-action failures and 2 invalid-output/sentinel failures. Thus **13 replaced attempts followed output/simulator-related termination**. v4's seven replaced folders all concern Thanksgiving setup. **No success followed an outer folder replacement in either arm**; extra outer retries did not increase the observed 6-versus-22 numerator. The internal SendWaiver setup recovery is the separate exception described in finding 3.
+
+**Fairness and remaining interpretation limits.** The defensible comparison is between these configured agent pipelines. It does not isolate model weights under equal inference resources. The container asymmetry is real: even the narrow inventory has GUI-Owl environment failures on eight tasks versus one for v4; the broader inventory is 18 versus three. Excluding known errors cannot establish that all scored tasks on either container were unaffected. A future controlled comparison should rotate/randomize container assignment or repeat both arms on matched fresh environments; do not “correct” scored failures selectively using their observed results.
